Concern: `inject()` inside async CanActivateFn before first await — fine, we call inject at top. Good.

Now components. Need write TS + HTML + SCSS for each. Let's carefully craft templates.

#### DynamicFieldComponent

TS:
```ts
import { ChangeDetectionStrategy, Component, input } from '@angular/core';
import { FormControl, ReactiveFormsModule } from '@angular/forms';
import type { FormFieldConfig, FormValue } from '../../core/models';
import { normalizeFieldValue } from './dynamic-form.factory';
import { vehicleYearBounds } from '../../core/validators/domain-validators';
import { UI_COPY } from '../../core/i18n/ui-copy';

@Component({ selector:'app-dynamic-field', imports:[ReactiveFormsModule], templateUrl, styleUrl, changeDetection: OnPush })
export class DynamicFieldComponent {
 readonly field = input.required<FormFieldConfig>();
 readonly control = input.required<FormControl<FormValue>>();
 readonly submitted = input(false);
 protected readonly copy = UI_COPY;

 isInvalid(): boolean {...}
 describedBy(): string | null {...}
 errorMessage(): string {...}
 onBlur(): void {...}
 numberMin(): string | null {...}
 numberMax(): string | null {...}
 autocomplete(): string {...}
 private todayBounds... 
}
```
Need `vehicleYearBounds()` returns object; call in template helper.

Note `[formControl]="control()"` requires ReactiveFormsModule imported. For `[attr.aria-invalid]` use string `'true'/'false'`; `boolean` would be converted to "true"/"false" anyway. Use method returning string.

For checkbox:
```html
<div class="checkbox-row">
 <input [id]="field().key" [formControl]="control()" type="checkbox" ... (blur)="onBlur()" />
 <label [for]="field().key">{{ field().label }}</label>
</div>
```
For non-checkbox label + control. Need `@switch` inside field body.

`aria-describedby` computed includes help id if helpText, error id if visible. Need error id exists only when error visible. Good.

`maxlength`/`minlength`: validators use Strapi; could add `[attr.maxlength]` etc but native attribute maybe okay; not required. Skip to avoid native validation surprises (novalidate on form).

For number min/max attributes: if rule vehicleYear, use helper bounds; else validations.min/max. Return string|null.

`inputmode="numeric"` for number and maybe text numeric document? not necessary.

`[attr.autocomplete]`: use method.

`type="date"` `[attr.min]`/`[attr.max]`.

`@if (field().helpText; as helpText)` — Angular `@if` alias works with expression; `field().helpText` type string|null; truthy string alias. fine.

#### WizardStepperComponent

TS with `input<WizardStep>('policyholder')`, copy.

#### StatePanelComponent

TS with `viewChild`, effect, output. Need imports ElementRef. `effect` in constructor reads `state()` and `heading()`; use untracked? Let's write:
```ts
constructor() {
 effect(() => {
  const state = this.state();
  const heading = this.heading();
  if (state !== 'loading' && heading) {
   queueMicrotask(() => heading.nativeElement.focus());
  }
 });
}
